 "relevance_note": "One of the 10 transplanted adults has HA20 with a listed TNFAIP3 variant: \"haploinsufficiency of A20 (HA20) (n = 1)\"; Table S1 row 9 gives \"TNFAIP3 (NM_001270508.2):p.Tyr306*\".",
 "method_note": "Single-centre cohort of 10 adults with IEI (and VEXAS) receiving alphabetaTCR/CD19-depleted allo-HSCT; only patient #9 (IEI HA20) is in scope; the other 9 (CTLA4, PIK3R1, DOCK8, FAS, ADA2, UBA1, TNFRSF13B) get no rows. Label: Table 1/2/S1 use a bare-number '#' column, but the text uses its own label ('Patient #9', 'patients #7 and #9'), so rule 1 gives 'Patient #9'. Table 1 'Age' (23) is age at allo-HSCT (text: 'Mean age at allo-HSCT was 32.1 (range 21-51)'), not onset, diagnosis or last evaluation, so all age fields are 'not reported'. Vital status left 'not reported': only patient #6 is named as having died and Table 2 marks only #6 with a dagger, but no sentence states that #9 is alive. Table S1 is a whitespace-aligned table from the supplementary PDF; the variant is printed protein-only with transcript (no cDNA); variant type, zygosity and inheritance are not stated. 'causal' comes from the Table S1 column header 'Causal genetic variant'. Not recorded as phenotypes: CMV/EBV serostatus (Pos/ Pos), IDDA scores (92 baseline, 24 at 1 year, '-' at latest follow-up), Karnofsky 40, HCT-CI 1, engraftment day 11, chimerism 100/100. Fig. S2 (clinical manifestations per patient) is only a figure, not available as text. Excluded rows: severe GvHD from the sentence naming patients #7 and #9; EBV reactivation (after depletion) and chronic GvHD from statements about all patients. No stacked ' / ' cells affect row 9 (the 'Pos/ Pos' cells are patient/donor pairs defined by the header; row 10's '5/100**' is not in scope). Contradiction (not about #9): Results say patients #5 and #8 showed mixed chimerism; Discussion says #5 and #6. Output built by a short Python script from values read by hand; spans checked verbatim by script.",
